<details id="search-info" name="search-panel" hidden>
  <summary aria-label="Search info" title="Search info">
    {% icon "informationCircle" %}
  </summary>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-words">
    <h2 id="search-info-words">Words</h2>
    <p>
      The best matches come first: a text's acronym, like
      <a href="/search?query=mn+19"><kbd>mn 19</kbd></a
      >, and its name count most, then its titles and headings, then the rest of
      its text. A whole word beats longer ones that start with it
    </p>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=four+noble+truths"
          ><kbd>four noble truths</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>Finds every word, anywhere in a text, in any order</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=%22four+noble+truths%22"
          ><kbd>"four noble truths"</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Finds all words together. Also works on each side of an <kbd>OR</kbd>
      </dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=monast"><kbd>monast</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Finds the start of a word too, and in English any ending, so
        <kbd>truth</kbd> finds “truths”
      </dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=savatthi"><kbd>savatthi</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Capitals and diacritics don't matter</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=greed+OR+desire"><kbd>greed OR desire</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Finds either word</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=greed+NOT+anicca"><kbd>greed NOT anicca</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Finds the first word, but not the second. A minus sign doesn't do this:
        <kbd>greed -anicca</kbd> finds both words
      </dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=greed+OR+desire+NOT+anicca"
          ><kbd>greed OR desire NOT anicca</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>Both together. <kbd>AND</kbd> works too, the same as a space</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-filters">
    <h2 id="search-info-filters">Filters</h2>
    <p>Each one ticks its box under Filters</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=by%3Asujato+cat"><kbd>by:sujato cat</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>By one translator or author</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=in%3Amn+monastery"><kbd>in:mn monastery</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>In one collection, by its SuttaCentral ID</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=in%3Aebt+free"><kbd>in:ebt free</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>
        In the early Buddhist texts. Or <kbd>in:ebs</kbd> for only the suttas,
        and <kbd>in:ebct</kbd> for only the Chinese. These are shortcuts, not a
        definitive list of what is early
      </dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=lang%3Apli+sati"><kbd>lang:pli sati</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>In one language, by its code</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=in%3Amn+by%3Asujato+Buddha+OR+monastery"
          ><kbd>in:mn by:sujato Buddha OR monastery</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>Filters and words together</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-include">
    <h2 id="search-info-include">Titles, notes and site pages</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=title%3Aintention"><kbd>title:intention</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Only the texts' titles</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=note%3Amindfulness"
          ><kbd>note:mindfulness</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>Only the translators' notes</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=site%3Aaggregates"><kbd>site:aggregates</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Only the site pages, like guides and essays. Same as
        <kbd>in:article aggregates</kbd>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-references">
    <h2 id="search-info-references">References</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=ref%3APTS+1.1"><kbd>ref:PTS 1.1</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Finds a reference number, ie <kbd>ref:sya13.544</kbd></dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=volpage%3ASN+ii+4"><kbd>volpage:SN ii 4</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Texts on a PTS volume and page, or a whole volume, ie
        <kbd>volpage:M II</kbd>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-lists">
    <h2 id="search-info-lists">Lists</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=list+authors"><kbd>list authors</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Every translator and author</dd>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=list+san"><kbd>list san</kbd></a>
      </dt>
      <dd>Every text in one language, by its code</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-chinese">
    <h2 id="search-info-chinese">Chinese</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>
        <a href="/search?query=in%3Aebct+%E5%9B%9B%E5%BF%B5%E8%99%95"
          ><kbd>in:ebct 四念處</kbd></a
        >
      </dt>
      <dd>
        Needs no spaces between words. The texts are in traditional characters,
        so search with those
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="search-info-one-word">
    <h2 id="search-info-one-word">One word</h2>
    <p>
      A search for one word shows its Pāli definitions, with a map for a place,
      and quick links to site pages, above the results. Either can be toggled
      under Filters, in “Show above results”
    </p>
  </section>
</details>
